<p>Wind damage insurance claims in San Marcos usually start the same way: a line of thunderstorms pushes through, gusts spike for a few minutes, and the next morning there are shingles in the yard, a fence leaning into the neighbor&rsquo;s lot, or a limb through the porch roof. The damage can look obvious, yet wind claims are frequently underpaid or questioned because the insurer reads the evidence differently. As a <a href="/">San Marcos Public Adjuster</a> serving Hays County, we help owners show clearly what the wind did and what it will cost to fix.</p>

<h2>Damaging Wind in the San Marcos Area</h2>
