<p>Notice that two of those entries involve metal roofs. Exposed-fastener panels on Hill Country homes, shops, and barns can lift at the edges once a gust gets underneath, and once one panel moves the rest of the run is at risk. Our article on <a href="/wind-damage-insurance-claims-san-marcos-tx/">wind damage insurance claims in San Marcos</a> covers more local history.</p>

<h2>What We Document After a Windstorm</h2>
<p>Wind leaves a pattern. Our inspection tries to capture that pattern so it is hard to dismiss as ordinary aging:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Shingles:</strong> creased or torn tabs, broken seal strips, missing pieces, and exposed nail heads, mapped by slope and compass direction.</li>
<li><strong>Metal roofing:</strong> lifted panel edges, pulled or backed-out fasteners, bent trim, and displaced ridge caps.</li>
<li><strong>Exterior:</strong> stripped siding, torn soffit and fascia, bent gutters, damaged fences, carports, and outbuildings.</li>
<li><strong>Tree damage:</strong> where the tree or limb struck, what it broke, and photographs before removal when it is safe.</li>
<li><strong>Interior:</strong> ceiling stains, wet insulation, and damaged drywall connected to a specific opening in the roof or wall.</li>
<li><strong>Weather data:</strong> NOAA and NWS reports for the date, which you can begin researching with our <a href="/storm-lookup/">storm lookup</a>.</li>
</ul>
