<h2>Where Wind Claims Run Into Trouble</h2>
<h3>&ldquo;Wear and tear&rdquo; denials</h3>
<p>Older shingles lose their seal over time, and insurers sometimes argue a roof would have failed anyway. A directional damage pattern on the windward side, recent storm reports, and neighbors with similar damage all help counter that argument.</p>
<h3>Wind-driven rain</h3>
<p>Many policies limit interior water damage unless wind first created an opening. If the claim photos show a stained ceiling but not the missing shingle above it, the interior portion may be denied.</p>
<h3>Partial roof scopes</h3>
<p>Insurers may approve a handful of replacement shingles on a roof where the remaining shingles have also lost their seal. Whether a broader repair is supported depends on the inspection findings and the policy.</p>
<h3>Deductibles and payment terms</h3>
<p>Because Hays County is outside the TWIA area, wind coverage comes from your regular insurer, often with a percentage wind/hail deductible. Roof payment schedules or ACV-only roof coverage can also reduce the check. See our <a href="/replacement-cost-vs-actual-cash-value-texas/">replacement cost versus ACV guide</a>.</p>

<h2>How We Handle a Wind Damage Claim</h2>
<ol>
<li>Free conversation and policy review, including your wind/hail deductible and any roof endorsements.</li>
<li>Full property inspection: roof, exterior elevations, fences, outbuildings, and interior.</li>
<li>Storm-date research and organized photo documentation.</li>
<li>Line-item estimate and submission to the insurer.</li>
<li>Meetings with the carrier&rsquo;s adjuster, responses to requests, and supplements as repairs reveal more.</li>
</ol>
<p>If you and the insurer agree the damage is covered but disagree on cost, appraisal may be available under the policy. Our <a href="/services/insurance-appraisal/">insurance appraisal</a> page explains how that works.</p>

<h2>When to Bring in a Public Adjuster</h2>
<p>A public adjuster in San Marcos can be helpful when the insurer called the damage pre-existing, when interior water damage was excluded, when a metal roof or multiple buildings are involved, or when the approved amount does not come close to contractor bids. If hail fell in the same storm, see our <a href="/services/hail-damage-claims/">hail damage claims</a> page, and for multi-peril events see <a href="/services/storm-damage-claims/">storm damage claims</a>. Start with a <a href="/free-claim-review/">free claim review</a> and we will tell you honestly whether we think we can add value.</p>
